  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Humid with additional showers/thunderstorms \npossible late today through the first half of tonight along and \nahead of a cold front moving south from New York state. \n\nA weak ridge of high pressure over Central PA this morning will\nmove east and off the New Jersey coast this afternoon allowing\nwarm, humid air to push northeast across the state this afternoon\nand evening. Light wind and the clearing of mid and high clouds\nacross the Northern Mtns early today will lead to areas of\nmainly light valley fog. Much of today will be partly to mostly\nsunny and dry, with a light NW breeze across the eastern half of\nthe state, and a light southwesterly breeze over the west -\nfreshening to around 10 kts this afternoon. \n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms will be possible this evening\nuntil shortly after midnight, along and just ahead of a cold front\nthat will be drifting south from New York State and a mid and\nupper level WNW jet max approaching from the Glakes region.\nHREF's MU CAPE rising to between 1000-1500 J/KG will create the\nopportunity for moderately strong updrafts and the potential \nfor some isolated wind damage from peak gusts of 40-45 kts and\nsmall hail.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Seasonably cooler and less humid Friday and\nSaturday \n\nComfortably cooler and noticeably drier (less humid) air \naccompanies seasonably strong/Canadian high pressure building \nsoutheast from the Upper Midwest Friday night through Saturday.  \n\nBelow normal pwats will facilitate pleasant days and crisp\nnights (40s and 50s most locations Friday night/AM Saturday).",
